:: Debate {"position":"400,25","size":"100,100"}
(set: $raisedConcern to true)
<div class="passage-shell" data-scene="office" data-typing="false"><div class="scene-hero" role="img" aria-label="An empty modern office at Amaze."></div><p class="photo-credit">Photo: <a href="https://www.pexels.com/photo/an-empty-office-5483236/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cottonbro studio / Pexels</a></p><div class="story-copy"><p class="kicker">03 / THE OBJECTION</p><h1>“It’s a choice they can change”</h1><p>You explain that a customer may see an immediate discount and overlook the monthly commitment. Choosing a delivery frequency for someone is different from asking what they need.</p><p>Morgan listens, but does not agree.</p><blockquote>“Subscriptions can help people who rely on deliveries, including customers who find shopping in person difficult. We give them convenience and a lower price.”</blockquote><p>You agree that subscriptions can be useful. You suggest letting customers choose whether to subscribe and how often they receive an item.</p><blockquote>“You’re new,” Morgan says. “Take a smaller project for now. We’ll revisit this.”</blockquote><div class="choices">
[[Take the smaller project while keeping your concern on record->SmallerProject]]
[[Agree to implement Sub and Save after the discussion->Implementation]]
</div></div></div>


